{"ts": 1789706453.3961742, "kind": "assistant_text", "text": "I've submitted my specification. Summary of my approach:\n\n1. **Screened all 40 individual features** with sign = +1 to get a baseline sense of signal strength.\n2. **Identified and avoided a trap**: features 11, 26, and 32 showed absurd in-sample Sharpe ratios (~50), and flipping signs simply flipped the sign of that huge Sharpe \u2014 a clear sign of look-ahead leakage/degenerate data rather than genuine predictive signal. Combining them pushed Sharpe even higher (~73), which would be a classic overfitting trap if chased blindly, since such magnitudes are not economically plausible and almost certainly won't survive out-of-sample.\n3. **Focused on the moderately strong, \"sane\" features** (Sharpes in the 0.3\u20130.5 range: features 2, 7, 12, 13, 23, 29, 36) and searched combinations of up to 3 with different signs.\n4. **Best found**: features **[2, 7, 29]**, all long (sign +1), giving an in-sample Sharpe of **0.834** \u2014 a solid, plausible combination without relying on the leakage artifacts.\n5. **Submitted** with a conservative predicted OOS Sharpe of **mean 0.45, sd 0.25**, reflecting expected shrinkage from in-sample to out-of-sample performance while still crediting genuine combined signal."}
